The Summer of Love is back in Monterey
Monterey is celebrating the 50th anniversary of the Monterey International Pop Festival with Summer of Love themed events all summer long.
The iconic festival brought together the likes of Jimmy Hendrix, The Who, and Janis Joplin in a first of it's kind outdoor concert. The event would kick off the Summer of Love and become the template for future outdoor festivals, including Woodstock in 1969.
Advertisement
The main event in the summer of 2017 will be the Monterey Pop Festival happening June 16-18, the first since the 1967 event. Headliners include Nora Jones, The Head and The Heart and Regina Spektor to name a few.
The anniversary bringing up fond memories for those who attended in 1967.
"We sat boxes over there and I didn't know what I was in for," said Monterey local John McCleary in an interview at the venue on Wednesday.
McCleary said the festival wasn't just a musical event it was a cultural event.
"I was changed by the experience, 67' was a different era to 68' to 69', everything changed," he said.
The festival embodied the spirit of the California Counter Culture and was the starting point for the Summer of Love that would take over neighborhoods like Haight Ashbury in San Francisco in the coming months.
"A lot of people may not know that the Monterey Pop Festival was the first outdoor festival, and sort of set the stage for other outdoor concerts," said Alliah Sheta with the Monterey County Convention and Visitors Bureau.
