The best things come to those who wait, and in this case the wait was nearly three decades and the best thing is Bananarama reuniting.
According the The Sun, the trio behind such 1980s classics as 'Venus', 'Cruel Summer', 'I Heard a Rumour', and 'Love In The First Degree' are coming back together to go on tour.
Keren Woodward, Sara Dallin and Siobhan Fahey last performed at the Brit Awards in 1988 before an acrimonious split – but have now re-joined forces for this reunion.
© Getty Images
Advertisement - Continue Reading Below
"We first had a chat about it over Christmas and before we knew it the whole thing snowballed. Keren and I called Siobhan to chat about it and things went from there," Sara told The Sun.
Siobhan apparently was unsure at first but eventually came around to the idea.
